  "notes": "Docker HB Shutdown Bug Core Fix — 5-sprint exit-137 bug (Sprint 134-138) resolved with 3-layer fix:\n\n(A) worker.ts — atomicWriteFileSync(): temp file → fsyncSync → renameSync (POSIX atomic rename, crash-safe). writeResult() now uses this instead of plain writeFileSync. Data guaranteed on disk after call returns.\n\n(B) worker.ts — SIGTERM handler enhanced: fsyncResultFile() called BEFORE finalizeHeartbeatOnShutdown(). Even if HB finalization fails, .result file is safe on disk. finalizeHeartbeatOnShutdown() also uses atomicWriteFileSync for HB.\n\n(C) spawn-backend-docker.ts — Grace period increased from 10s to 15s. Worker script now defines POSIX-portable fsync_file() shell function (dd conv=fsync + mv). Both EXIT and TERM traps call fsync_file on .result and .hb files. kill() method adds post-stop verifyResultAfterStop() with host-side fsync. monitorContainer() adds host-side fsync before .result reconciliation read.\n\n(D) 21 new tests in tests/e2e/docker-hb-shutdown.test.ts covering: atomicWriteFileSync (4 tests), fsyncResultFile (3 tests), writeResult atomic pattern (3 tests), finalizeHeartbeatOnShutdown (6 tests), worker script trap verification (2 tests), Docker backend graceful stop (3 tests). All pass. Existing worker.test.ts mocks updated for new fs imports (fsyncSync, renameSync) — 61 tests still pass. Docker backend tests pass (9 skipped due to no Docker daemon in CI).\n\ntsc --noEmit: only pre-existing error in sprint-finalizer.ts (out of scope). Our changes compile cleanly.",
